# Environment Configuration Examples

## Backend (.env)

```bash
# Flask Configuration
FLASK_ENV=development
FLASK_DEBUG=true

# Interactive Brokers Connection
IB_HOST=127.0.0.1
IB_PORT=7497              # Paper trading port
IB_CLIENT_ID=100
PAPER_TRADING=true

# Strategy Configuration
AUTO_BUY_SHARES=false     # Don't auto-buy for rounding
MIN_SHARES_REQUIRED=100
POLL_SECONDS=20

# Option Bot Settings
VIX_HIGH_LEVEL=30         # Risk threshold
VIX_CAUTION_LEVEL=22
CAPITAL_PROTECTION_ENABLED=true

# Data Files
BOT_TRADES_CSV=bot_trades.csv
CONFIG_FILE=data/user_config.json

# logging
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
```

## Frontend (.env.local - Development)

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL=60000  # ms
```

## Frontend (.env.production)

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-api-domain.com/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL=60000
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=your-analytics-id
```

## Deployment Environments

### Railway
Set these in Railway dashboard:
```
FLASK_ENV=production
IB_HOST=127.0.0.1
IB_PORT=7497
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-project-name.up.railway.app/api
```

### Vercel
Set in Project Settings → Environment Variables:
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-api-domain.com/api
```

### Heroku
```bash
heroku config:set IB_PORT=7497 IB_HOST=127.0.0.1
heroku config:set FLASK_ENV=production
```

## Never Commit

- `.env` files (local secrets)
- `*.key` or credentials
- IBKR authentication details
- API keys

Use `.env.example` template instead:
```bash
# .env.example
IB_HOST=127.0.0.1
IB_PORT=7497
IB_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID_HERE
```
